## Implement Path Deletion Logic

The `delete` function has been implemented to satisfy all requirements. It parses the path, rejects empty paths and wildcards, navigates to the parent of the last segment (raising `PathError` if any intermediate step is missing or invalid), and then removes the value from the parent `dict` or `list`. For lists, it handles negative indices by validating the range before calling `pop`, ensuring that only existing elements are deleted. If the parent is not a supported container type or the value is missing, appropriate `PathError`s are raised.

